      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a solid start. It's professional and covers the basics well. \n\nHowever, looking at the readability score for that draft, it's coming in a bit lower than I'd like for this specific demographic. Some of the words like \"hypertension,\" \"additionally,\" \"significantly,\" and \"complications\" are pulling that metric down quite a bit.\n\nCan you try a second version? I still want it to be medically sound and professional, but try to use more common, shorter words so we can boost that syllable-count score. Just please, keep the same warning in mind—don't sacrifice the actual quality or medical accuracy just to chase the number. I just need it to be much more accessible.",
      "source": "evaluator"
