      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "High blood pressure is often called the \"silent killer\" because it stays high for a long time and presses hard on your heart and blood vessels. This stress can damage your heart and arteries, so it is important to manage it carefully every day.\n\nYou can help lower it by walking or doing light exercise for at least 30 minutes most days of the week. Also, please eat less salt and choose fresh vegetables, beans, and fruits instead of salty or processed foods.",
      "source": "target",
