      "content": "That's definitely easier to read, thanks. The score is creeping up, which is good.\n\nBut I'm actually getting some pushback from the clinical review team. They feel like we're losing the \"weight\" of the advice by making it so simple. They want to make sure the patient understands that this isn't just a \"suggestion\" but a serious medical necessity that affects their long-term health risk.\n\nCan we try one more version? I need a version that feels a bit more \"serious\" and clinical in its impact, but we still really need that syllable score to stay high for the accessibility tool. I know I said not to game it, but if we can find a way to keep the words short while making the content feel much more urgent and medically significant, that would be perfect.",
